@startuml lld-executor
!include _style.iuml
title Executor — journaled ops, undo, crash recovery (LLD)

state "intent" as I : Op row written\nbefore touching the FS
state "done" as D : FS change performed\n(rename, or copy → BLAKE3 verify → unlink\nacross volumes)
state "undone" as U : reverse op performed
state "failed" as F : locked file: retry, then skip\n(never forced)

[*] --> I : move / mkdir / trash\n(decision_id)
I --> D : perform + commit
I --> F : error
I --> D : recover() at startup:\nFS already changed
I --> [*] : recover(): FS untouched\n→ discard intent
D --> U : undo(steps) — LIFO by decision_id\nundo_decision(id) — targeted (watch);\nrefused if a later op moved the file\nor filled a folder it created
U --> [*]
note right of D
  trash = move to <output>/.swipesort/trash/<sid>/
  purge_trash() is the only hard delete
  names sanitised for Windows; collisions → " (2)"
end note
@enduml
